  {
    "type": "updateEntity",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "6cca7447555640cb911a65702a9a3eb6"
    },
    "set": [
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "## Coverage and interpretation\n\nThe current table contains the authors' pooled life-cycle, all-benefits model estimate: benefit/cost ratio 7.33, standard error 1.84. It is one specification from Table 6 of the August 2, 2018 author manuscript, not an independent third experiment. [Source manuscript](https://cehd.uchicago.edu/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/abc_comprehensivecba_revised_2018-08-02a_jlg.pdf).\n\n## Comparison assumptions\n\nThe baseline discounts benefits and costs to birth at 3% and forecasts through age 79. The reported ratio averages bootstrap ratios; it is not necessarily the ratio of rounded aggregate means. Control childcare substitution costs enter the authors' benefits accounting. Forecasts combine experimental and nonexperimental data.\n\n## Cost caveat\n\nThe 2018 appendix's listed annual cost components do not reconcile to its reported total. Author-reported estimates are preserved; independently reconstructed cost-effectiveness rankings remain unresolved. The two underlying trials and alternate forecast specifications must not be counted as independent replications.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "unset": []
  },
